  "formal_result": "PrimeCheckpoints R implies the unmodified Mathlib RiemannHypothesis. The hypothesis explicitly supplies cofinally small finite rational costs and valid bids on the retained grid. The proof caps the removed mass and transports old values on the same grid.",
  "paper_result": [
    "Critical maxima of the ordinary-prime discrepancy control the old maxima at every cutoff.",
    "The accumulated discrepancy controls the actual signed-edge area with at most a two-thirds power of a logarithm of the side.",
    "Both signs of a logarithmically amplified critical oscillation remain after any fixed cut at both ends."
  ],
  "open": "Establish the required subpower growth of the retained comparisons for the actual integer inputs. The new native replays certify the conditional implication. The independent Comparator receipt on the prior signed-area implication remains separate."
